--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Eldamo - An Elvish Lexicon
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Quenya and Sindarin vocabulary embedded in the binary (data/quenya.bin,
data/sindarin.bin and the Elvish side of data/lex.*) is derived from
eldamo-data.xml, version 0.8.13, https://eldamo.org

  (c) 2008 - 2026, Paul Strack.
  This work is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
  International License (CC BY 4.0),
  http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Changes: entries were extracted with tools/eldamo_extract.py, filtered to
Neo-Quenya / Neo-Sindarin words, reduced to (word, gloss, part of speech,
stem, inflection notes) tuples and re-encoded into the binary formats
defined in crates/tkdata.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Wiktionary (via wiktextract / kaikki.org)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The multilingual lexicon (all non-English languages -> English lemma
mappings, English lemma inventory, part-of-speech tag sets, function-word
lists, language name tables) embedded in data/lex.*, data/en.*,
data/en_keys.*, data/lists.*, data/tagsets.bin, data/erank.bin and
data/langs.bin is derived from the English Wiktionary
(https://en.wiktionary.org) as machine-readable JSON produced by the
wiktextract project and published at https://kaikki.org
(raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl).

  Wiktionary text is available under the Creative Commons
  Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported License (CC BY-SA 3.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
  and the GNU Free Documentation License.

  wiktextract: Copyright (c) 2018-2024 Tatu Ylonen, MIT License.

Changes: glosses were parsed into head lemmas (tools/kaikki_*.py,
tools/glossparse.py), ranked, deduplicated and re-encoded into the binary
formats defined in crates/tkdata. The derived data files are therefore
also made available under CC BY-SA 3.0.

